CAT = "s65Ethics"; SEG = "ETH"
Q = [
("An investment adviser's fiduciary duty to its clients consists of a duty of care and a duty of:", 'Loyalty', ['Profit', 'Confidentiality only', 'Best execution only'], "Advisers owe clients a duty of care (advice in the client's best interest, best execution, monitoring) and a duty of loyalty (put the client first and disclose conflicts)."),
('An adviser requires clients to prepay substantial fees six or more months in advance. As a result it must:', 'Include a balance sheet', ['Refund the fees each quarter', 'Register with the SEC', 'Stop charging fees in advance'], 'Advisers that require large prepayments six or more months ahead must give clients an audited balance sheet with their disclosure, since clients are creditors of the firm.'),
('An advisory firm organized as a partnership admits a new minority partner. Under the Act it must:', 'Notify its clients', ["Get every client's consent", 'Re-sign all contracts', 'Do nothing at all'], 'Contracts of a partnership adviser must require it to tell clients of any change in membership within a reasonable time. A change of the majority is an assignment that needs consent.'),
("An adviser without custody receives a client's stock certificate in the mail by mistake. To avoid having custody, it should:", 'Return it to the sender promptly', ['Keep it in the office safe', 'Deposit it in its own account', 'Hold it until the client visits'], 'Inadvertently received client securities are not custody if the adviser promptly returns them to the sender, and keeps a record of doing so.'),
('An adviser charges 1% a year of the assets it manages. Which statement is true?', 'It is not a performance fee', ['It needs qualified clients', 'It is a prohibited fee', 'It must be refunded yearly'], 'A fee figured as a percentage of assets averaged over a period is not a performance fee, so it may be charged to any client. A share of capital gains is a performance fee.'),
("A new client receives the adviser's brochure 24 hours before signing the advisory contract. The client:", 'May cancel within 5 business days', ['Has no right to cancel', 'May cancel within 90 calendar days', 'May cancel only with a penalty'], 'When the brochure is delivered less than 48 hours before the contract is signed, the client may end the contract without penalty within five business days.'),
("An IAR's website says she holds a professional designation she never earned. This is:", 'Misrepresenting qualifications', ['Fine if she is studying for it', 'Puffery, not a violation', 'Allowed with a disclaimer'], "Misrepresenting an adviser's or IAR's qualifications, or the nature of its services or fees, is an unethical practice and fraud."),
("An adviser's written business continuity plan should mainly address:", 'Disaster recovery and succession', ['Raising fees during a market downturn', 'Marketing to new clients', 'Choosing a fund benchmark'], "NASAA's model rule asks state-registered advisers to plan for disruptions such as natural disasters, cyber attacks and the death or disability of key people, including succession."),
('A dual-registered rep acts as both an IAR and a broker-dealer agent for the same client. When recommending a product, she must make clear:', 'Which capacity she is in', ['Only her commission rate', "Nothing, since she's registered", 'Her personal net worth'], 'Dual registrants owe a fiduciary duty as advisers and a best interest duty as brokers, so they must tell clients which role they are acting in and the conflicts that follow.'),
('An adviser pays higher commissions in exchange for research from a broker. Clients must be told about this in:', 'The Form ADV brochure', ['A FINRA filing', 'A press release', 'Only if a client asks'], 'Soft-dollar arrangements are a conflict of interest, so the adviser must describe them in Part 2A of Form ADV, the brochure delivered to clients.'),
('A fee-based adviser also earns commissions on insurance products she recommends to advisory clients. She must:', 'Disclose the conflict', ['Stop charging advisory fees', 'Rebate all commissions', 'Register as an insurer'], 'Receiving more than one kind of pay for the same advice is a conflict of interest that must be disclosed, so the client can judge the recommendation.'),
('An adviser is authorized to deduct its fees directly from client accounts held at a custodian. For state purposes, the adviser:', 'Has custody', ['Has no custody', 'Is a broker-dealer', 'Is a qualified custodian'], 'Authority to withdraw client funds, including fee deduction, is custody. It triggers safeguards such as written authorization and statements from the custodian.'),
("An adviser has written discretion over a conservative retiree's account and buys speculative options in it. This is:", 'Unsuitable for her goals', ['Allowed, since it has discretion', 'Allowed if the trade profits', 'Required to diversify her'], "Discretion lets the adviser choose trades without asking each time, but every trade must still fit the client's objectives, risk tolerance and investment policy."),
("A new client brings cash in several deposits, each just under the currency reporting threshold, and won't say where it came from. The adviser should:", 'Treat it as suspicious and escalate', ['Accept it, since each deposit is small', 'Ask the client to use checks', 'Tell the client about the threshold'], "Breaking cash into amounts below the reporting threshold is structuring, a classic money laundering red flag. The firm's AML procedures call for escalation and possible suspicious activity reporting, without tipping off the client."),
('An adviser that is also a broker-dealer wants to sell a bond to an advisory client from its own inventory. It must:', 'Get consent before completion', ['Get consent within 30 days after', 'Never do so under any terms', 'Tell the client only if asked'], "Acting as principal in an advisory account requires written disclosure of the capacity and the client's consent before the transaction is completed."),
('In an agency cross transaction, the adviser arranges a trade between an advisory client and a brokerage customer. Which is prohibited?', 'Recommending it to both sides', ["Getting the client's prior consent", 'Sending a trade confirmation', 'Disclosing its compensation'], 'Agency cross trades are allowed with prior written consent and disclosure, but the adviser may not recommend the transaction to both the buyer and the seller.'),
("Under NASAA's model rule, an adviser may lend money to a client only if:", 'It is a lender or she is an affiliate', ['The client signs a note', 'The loan is short-term', 'The rate is fair'], 'Lending to a client is unethical unless the adviser is a financial institution in the business of lending or the client is an affiliate of the adviser.'),
("A client's ex-husband calls asking for her account balance. The adviser should:", 'Decline without her consent', ['Share it if he knows her SSN', 'Share it if they were married long', 'Send the latest statement'], 'Client information is confidential and may be shared only with consent, as required by law (such as a subpoena), or as allowed in the privacy notice.'),
('Under federal law, every investment adviser must keep and enforce written policies that:', 'Prevent misuse of inside information', ['Guarantee market-beating returns', 'Ban all personal trading', 'Require trades through one broker'], 'The Insider Trading and Securities Fraud Enforcement Act requires advisers and broker-dealers to establish, keep and enforce written policies to prevent the misuse of material nonpublic information.'),
('An adviser buys a thinly traded stock for its own account, recommends it to clients to lift the price, then sells its shares. This is:', 'Scalping', ['Front running', 'Selling away', 'Churning'], 'Scalping is buying ahead of your own recommendation and selling into the price rise it causes. It is fraud and a form of market manipulation.'),
("An adviser's access persons must report their own securities holdings when they join and their trades every quarter. This is required by:", 'The code of ethics rules', ["FINRA's suitability rule", 'The Investment Company Act', "ERISA's fiduciary rules"], 'SEC Rule 204A-1 requires a code of ethics with initial and annual holdings reports and quarterly transaction reports from access persons. States apply similar rules.'),
("An adviser's executive donates to a candidate for state treasurer, an office that hires managers for the state pension. Under pay-to-play rules, the adviser may face:", 'A two-year compensation ban', ['A permanent license revocation', 'A one-time small fine', 'No restriction at all'], 'Pay-to-play rules bar an adviser from being paid by a government client for two years after a covered associate makes a contribution above a de minimis level to an official who can influence its selection.'),
('An adviser charges a percentage-of-assets fee on a client account it almost never reviews or trades. This may be:', 'Reverse churning', ['Churning', 'Best execution', 'Scalping'], "Placing a client who needs little service in a fee-based account, and charging for management that is not provided, is called reverse churning and may breach the adviser's duty."),
("An adviser believes an 85-year-old client is being pressured by a relative to drain her account. Under laws based on NASAA's model act, the adviser may:", 'Report it and delay payment', ['Close the account at once', 'Freeze it indefinitely', "Do nothing, as it's private"], "NASAA's model act for vulnerable adults lets qualified individuals report suspected financial exploitation to the state and delay a disbursement for a limited period."),
]
